style: move activity page styles onto design tokens

Add public/tokens.css with the tokens from 01-foundations that the
activity page uses (palette tokens plus the semantic tokens that point at
them), link it before activity.css, and rewrite activity.css to reference
semantic tokens only.

Why: the filter work that follows needs tokenized styles, and the old
sheet had raw hex values and px sizes that would fail review. Panel and
table styles now match the "Token use by surface" table in 01 (panel
border and shadow, sunken table header, row padding, tabular numbers).

Notes for review:
- max-width is 60rem (was 960px). 01 has no max-width token; happy to
  add one in a separate docs: commit.
- Each --type-* token is a font shorthand; tracking is a companion
  --type-*-tracking token because 01 does not say how to encode them.

Checked: grep finds no raw hex or px in activity.css; page rendered in
headless Chrome at 1200px wide and the table, header, and panel look as
expected.

